; The owner's session at CART.12's hand test, recorded 2026-10-19 in the page at rate 0, the cartridge
; loaded with the seed the page chose, each act stepped to its settle's end: the first observation by a
; press on L11, a reading of nothing whose cascade opened 22 sites; a press on U16, a reading of one; the
; command box on U16, which leaves a reading as it stands, and on V21, a box sealed on a reading of nothing;
; the command collapse on AC21 and AD17, sites in superposition, which it leaves as they stand; the command
; observe on M17, E34 and J34, two cascades among them, the first reaching the box on V21 at frame 33 and
; opening it, since nothing has decayed beside nothing; then nine presses, two of them decays observed (AP23
; and Q46), and at S56 the session's deepest cascade, 30 settle steps opening 288 sites. 18 acts over 118
; frames in one world, 635 sites observed, two decays and no box at its end; a settle's frames hold no row.
; Recorded on the cartridge of the first hand test, its lattice at B2, and carried onto this one as Sand's
; first replay was (CART.2): its header renamed to this cartridge's digest, and each act's place moved a row
; up and a column left with the lattice, which the second hand test moved to A1, the load's first rows as
; the host writes them; so every act stands on the site it was made on, in the world it was dealt, the
; decays' hash keeping each site's world. Under the first hand test's rule the box on V21 stayed sealed
; inside the opening, the owner's finding at the second. It replaces the stand-in, the floors' scripted
; player's session (CART.12, decision 7). Its golden is the Tally's row sums at its last frame, each
; decoding into its row's observations, boxes and decays.
; Re-stamped 2026-10-29 at ENGINE.28's close, the Field and the Observer the game's and read-only and the
; Constants a person's, a manifest's directives, and again after it for the sites' grid, an edge on
; each look's format; none moves a cell the session writes or reads.
